d to it  we did we did we perfected it actually  before she got involved we knew the game  was going to work what we didn't know  was exactly you know the phenomenon be  it would become but I had a sneaking  suspicion that it could be something  rather special what was how did you you  know get in touch with her how did you  get her involved in the project well we  were looking you know 2012 I thought  long and hard about the future of  Hollywood the future of glue and I  actually went went to Hollywood and did  a couple innovative seminal partnership  deals  we're doing a James Bond movie  game we're doing a terminator game and  Kim was one of these three deals that we  did all of this is impacting now so  Kim's game launched last summer we have  two or three more games that are  exciting with Hollywood this year and  Kim you know I started working with  probably in early 2013 believe it or not  when we started discussing what the  concept could be I went originally  through William Morris which was her  agent right but she got the concept  immediately and I knew we were onto a  good thing because she actually is an  authentic presence with all her social  channels and I knew it could be even  more authentic through a game which in a  lot of ways if you think about it  Kim builds a lot of value for Twitter  and Facebook and so on  you know indirectly her own game is  something that is her brand and so by  spending more time like coming like glue  she's actually building long-term brand  equity for herself now when you're SEC  filings you guys talk about building the  company as a gaming as a service yeah  what does that mean game is a service  that's a great question and we'll talk  more about it I think this morning games  today on phones are not you know single  download short s-curve wonder is like  going to see a movie or going to  download a DVD ultimately we're building  services that look more like annuities  more like a web portal you know Yahoo's  in what 